=== Python: and/or return an OPERAND ===
  True and "hello"       -> 'hello'      (type str)
  False and "hello"      -> False        (type bool)
  "" or "fallback"       -> 'fallback'   (type str)
  0 or "fallback"        -> 'fallback'   (type str)
  "a" or "b"             -> 'a'          (type str)

=== A boolean-only language would give ===
  True and "hello"       -> True
  False and "hello"      -> False
  "" or "fallback"       -> True
  0 or "fallback"        -> True
  "a" or "b"             -> True
